  "theorem_contract": {
    "euclidean_volume_inflation": "The volume of the n-dimensional Euclidean ball of radius R = sqrt(n) containing the true binary witness scales asymptotically as Vol(B_n(sqrt(n))) = (2 pi e)^{n/2} / sqrt(pi n) = 2^{2.0471 n - 0.5 log2(pi n)}.",
    "density_one_point_multiplicity": "At density d = 1.0 (modulus D = 2^n), the expected number of integer lattice points inside B_n(sqrt(n)) is N_points = Vol(B_n(sqrt(n))) / 2^n = (2.0664)^n / sqrt(pi n) = 2^{1.0471 n - 0.5 log2(pi n)} = 2^{Omega(n)}.",
    "bdd_radius_collapse": "By the Gaussian heuristic, the BDD unique decoding radius is R_BDD = lambda_1 / 2 approx 0.242 sqrt(n). The true binary witness has norm ||e||_2 = sqrt(n) approx 4.13 R_BDD, placing it far outside the unique BDD decoding ball.",
    "list_undercoverage": "Any nearest-plane or sphere-decoding list decoder exploring a polynomial list of size L = poly(n) achieves coverage bounded by P_coverage <= poly(n) / 2^{1.047 n} = 2^{-Omega(n)}, factorially/exponentially suppressing all Euclidean lattice approaches."
  },
