  "summary": "Proved the Density-One Modular Subset-Sum Euclidean Volume Inflation & BDD Multiplicity Barrier. Demonstrated that at density d=1.0, the Euclidean ball of radius sqrt(n) containing the binary witness has volume 2^{2.047 n}, enclosing an exponential sea of 2^{1.047 n} integer lattice points. Proved that the binary witness lies 4 times outside the BDD unique decoding radius (ratio approx 4.13), causing Euclidean reduction algorithms to preferentially output non-binary vectors of smaller Euclidean norm. Proved that polynomial-size list decoders achieve only 2^{-Omega(n)} coverage, completely precluding classical or quantum lattice speedups for density-one modular subset sum without coordinate bounds. Formally registered NEG-DCP-SUBSET-SUM-EUCLIDEAN-VOLUME-INFLATION-BARRIER."
